  "chapter": {
    "number": 80,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(81) For the end, a Psalm for",
          {
            "noteId": 149
          },
          "Asaph, concerning the wine presses."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Rejoice you⌃ in God our helper; shout aloud to the God of Jacob.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Take a psalm, and produce the timbrel, the pleasant lute with the harp.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Blow the trumpet at the new moon, in the glorious day of",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 150
          },
          {
            "text": "your feast.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For this is an ordinance for Israel, and a statute of the God of Jacob.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He made",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 151
          },
          {
            "text": "it to be a testimony in Joseph, when he came forth out of the land of Egypt: he heard a language which he understood not.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "He removed his back from burdens: his hands slaved in making the baskets.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You did call upon me in trouble, and I delivered you; I heard you in the secret place of the storm: I proved you at the water of",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 152
          },
          {
            "text": "Strife. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Hear, my people, and I will speak to you, O Israel; and I will testify to you: if you will listen to me;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "there shall be no new god in you; neither shall you worship a strange god.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For I am the Lord your God, that brought you out of the land of Egypt: open your mouth wide, and I will fill it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "But my people listened not to my voice; and Israel gave no heed to me.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "So I let them go after the ways of their own hearts: they will go on in their own ways.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "If my people had listened to me, if Israel had walked in my ways,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "I should have put down their enemies very quickly, and should have laid my hand upon those that afflicted them.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The Lord's enemies should have lied to him: but",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 153
          },
          {
            "text": "their time shall be for ever.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And he fed them with the fat of wheat; and satisfied them with honey out of the rock.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 149,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Alex. David.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 80,
          "verse": 0
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 150,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Alex. our.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 80,
          "verse": 3
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 151,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Gr. him, sc. Israel.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 80,
          "verse": 5
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 152,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Lit. contradiction.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 80,
          "verse": 7
        }
      },
      {
        "noteId": 153,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "sc. of the others.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 80,
          "verse": 15
        }
      }
